From 32ab7ed8d59603d5aca77fb1338f6cb1c8314ef2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Ron D." <8740514+rgnv@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 14:45:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 21/29] server+menu: browser lobby host can start the match

The game-setup screen's Start button now works for a remote (dedicated
server) lobby host: the menu relays lobby_start_match to the server via
the clc_stringcmd channel, and the server accepts lobby-mutating string
commands (lobby_config / lobby_slot / lobby_start_match) only from the
lobby host - the lowest-numbered connected client (the in-process
loopback client on a listen server). The host flag travels in
svc_lobby_setup right after local_slot so the setup screen enables the
Start button only for the host; single-line commands are relayed via
mi.ServerCommand while a local listen host keeps executing locally.

Tests: server_net gains lobby_start_match_is_host_gated (non-host
ignored, host start leaves the lobby); suites green (server_net
3239/3239, menu 1433/1433).

Also guard the game module's gi-fallback host services for emscripten
only: the native module cannot link engine-level symbols (MemAlloc /
FS_ReadFileQ3), which silently broke the native test-link of libgame.
